weightings where the two rules disagree: 1 of 3

reading
  The improvement is available only under the generation order. A
  hand-written table records a winner somebody read off a findings
  file, and a findings file reports medians. A generator holds the
  samples, so it can pick the section a rerun is most likely to
  reproduce instead of the section this run happened to produce.

  It is a small win and it is cheap to keep: the generator already has
  the samples, and the extra cost is resampling them once, offline, at
  the moment the table is written. It costs nothing at compile time and
  nothing at run time, which is the bound on taking a win.

  What it does NOT do is make the section stable. The modal section for
  the least stable weighting is still reproduced by only a minority of
  resamples, so the underlying instability is a property of the
  measurement rather than of the selection rule. Choosing the modal one
  makes the shipped answer the most likely one; it does not make it
  likely.
